  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Blend bread crumbs, cheese, parsley, salt and pepper. Set aside.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine melted butter and garlic.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Dip chicken into butter mixture, then in bread crumb mixture.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Roll each chicken breast into a firm roll.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Arrange in a baking pan or glass casserole dish.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Drizzle lemon juice and remaining butter over chicken.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake at 350 for 45 minutes or until tender.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "COMMENTS (from Adele)",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "If you can find breast fillets, they are easier to work with than the breasts. If you start with breasts, you may want to cut them in half or in thirds lengthwise to make it easier to roll them. (Freezing the chicken breasts slightly makes them easier to cut). Another option is to pound each breast to make them thinner. I added ¼ cup of white wine to the remaining butter and lemon juice before drizzling the mixture over the chicken rolls.",
      "group": null
    }
